text:
marisol (partnerships): Heads-up: TerraChip sent a creative pack for our joint solution brief + marketplace tile. Theyre asking for a thermal-badge overlay and a PCIe icon on the hero diagram. Timeline: marketplace preview next week.

uploadbot (system): Uploaded: TerraChip_CoBrand_Pack_v1.zip to /partnerships/terrachip/2410001234 12312hash.

tom (design): opening files now. initial thoughts: 1) their thermal-badge (red rounded rectangle) sits over product art and will obscure callouts at small sizes. recommend alternate placement below the fold for 300x300 tiles. 2) PCIe icon needs 24px grid alignment with our icon set for visual parity. 3) request vector .svg for the badge and the icon.

marisol (partnerships): They only provided PNGs and a layered sketch file. I can ask for SVGs but want to know if our team can produce a vendor-approved SVG from their master.

lina (legal): Before we redraw anything, we need explicit permission to modify iconography or produce new vectors. Clause 5.1 says partners can't alter trademark marks without written ok. Ask TerraChip for a short written license to produce a marketplace-optimized SVG and to place the thermal-badge outside of functional diagrams.

jake (product): From product side: the hero diagram shows on-prem inference with a PCIe-attached Redwood Dedicated appliance. PCIe icon must not imply TerraChip hardware is required; add text: "Compatible with common PCIe accelerators" next to the icon. Also, can we get a 15-word byline for the tile and a 1-sentence lead for the solution brief?

marisol (partnerships): I'll request the SVG and the permissions now. Also ask TerraChip to provide a signed short quote from their field engineer for the brief.

tom (design): If TerraChip doesn't supply SVGs, we can trace high-res PNGs and create matching icons, but we'll flag it to legal as derivative work. For marketplace thumbnails: recomend background-safe padding at 10% and swap the thermal-badge to a corner lockup. Example CSS snippet for thumbnail layout:

```css
.tile {
  padding: 10%;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
}
.badge {
  position: absolute;
  right: 12px;
  bottom: 12px;
  min-width: 48px;
}
```

lina (legal): Also request trademark attribution: "TerraChipis a registered trademark of TerraChip, Inc." Include the rights line in the case PDF and get sign-off on edits. If they approve vector recreation, require a short addendum granting Redwood permission to publish optimized assets in marketplace contexts.

marisol (partnerships): TerraChip responded: they can provide SVGs for the PCIe icon but not for the thermal-badge; they allow a resized badge if not recolored. Theyve given a one-line quote from their engineer: "Redwood's runtime simplified our hybrid deployment." Do we edit?

jake (product): Edit to hero-safe copy: "Made hybrid inference simpler across cloud and edge." That's tighter. Good for 15-word tile? maybe expand: "TerraChip and Redwood simplified hybrid inference, enabling low-latency on-prem throughput with cloud-managed rollouts."

lina (legal): Edit of quote is okay if we keep intent. Add rights lines and obtain signature on the quote. I'll draft the addendum: permission to produce marketplace-optimized vectors for thumbnails and diagrams, non-exclusive, revocable with 30-day notice.

tom (design): I'll prepare two sets of assets: 1) marketplace tile pack (SVG/PNG at 300, 600, 1200 px) with badge in corner; 2) solution brief hero (full bleed, thermal-badge below annotations). Will include alt text and a single-line accessibility caption for the PCIe icon: "PCIe accelerator connector".

marisol (partnerships): Target: final assets and signed addendum by Wednesday noon so the marketplace preview can go live Friday. I'll push checklist and update TerraChip. :rocket:

uploadbot (system): Shared drive link: https://drive.company/partnerships/terrachip/2410001234 - TerraChip_CoBrand_Pack_v1.zip

jake (product): thumbs up. i'll validate the copy in the staging marketplace once assets are uploaded.

lina (legal): I'll circulate the addendum for signature and post approval here.

tom (design): noted. I'll flag any layout issues if TerraChip's SVGs differ visually from our system icons.

marisol (partnerships): thanks team. i'll confirm once signed and upload the final checklist to the Figma file. :white_check_mark:
